    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0886" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v24/pg862"/>

                <head>407. Memorandum From President Kennedy to His Special Assistant for National
                    Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d407-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-07-03">July 3,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I do not want any further assistance to go to the Laotian Government unless it is
                    cleared here first.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d407-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d407-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Countries Series, Laos:
                    General, 7/1/62–7/16/62. The memorandum was not signed or initialed by Kennedy.
                    Bundy wrote the following note on the source text: “done &amp; understood.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
